          Granite is one of the hardest natural stones in the world — but it's also porous. Every kitchen spill that hits an unsealed granite countertop is a tiny race between you and capillary action. Win the race and you wipe up the spill. Lose the race and you have a permanent dark spot in your $4,000 countertop. The right sealer makes the race irrelevant. After 12 months of testing, here's what actually works.
